WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:01.801
Having the quote, we're

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.236
having a normal call.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.471
Nobody said, Oh, gee,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.538
he shouldn't have said that.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.340
What if this call was bad?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.075
I question the election.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.543
This guy's bad.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.212
I didn't ask him to find anything.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.848
We just heard the audio of this call.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.717
So, look, all I want to do is this.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:20.520
I just want to find

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:25.592
11,718 votes,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.328
which is one more that we have

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.864
because we won the state.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.732
The video you just saw was former

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.933
President Trump last night

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.302
denying asking Georgia's Republican

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.637
Secretary of State, Brad

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.773
Raffensperger, to find him votes

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.507
before conceding

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.809
that he did ask him to find him votes.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.077
And then the audio you just heard

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:44.544
was then

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.147
President Trump in January of 2021

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.983
directly asking Raffensperger to find him

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:50.984
those votes.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.785
Joining us now,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.452
Georgia Secretary

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.120
of State Brad Raffensperger.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.954
Thank you so much, Mr.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.057
Secretary, for joining us tonight.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.292
What was your reaction when you heard

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.827
those comments last night?

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:04.631
Well, President

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.165
Trump

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.767
said we didn't hang up on the phone call.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.536
You have to understand,

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.470
I've been taught

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.138
and I believe in respecting people's

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.540
positional authority

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.507
no matter what that level

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.909
and what office they hold.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.343
But he held the office

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.112
of president of united states of america

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.247
and that office deserves respect.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.016
Whenever you have a conversation

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:23.650
with the president

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.552
of the United States of America.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:25.885
So.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.153
So that's why you didn't hang up,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.456
not because you did.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:30.123
What was it

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.424
he was essentially suggesting?

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.625
Was that if you and your attorneys

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.893
who were on the call,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.427
I should note,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.762
which was also recorded,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.230
actually thought something was wrong,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:37.764
that you would have

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.665
hung up in the moment.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:39.532
But you were saying you did it

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.700
because it was the president

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.168
of the United States on the other line.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:44.971
I wouldn't hang up on

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.005
a governor, Senator.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.173
Congress per person.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.108
I just respect people's

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.609
position of authority.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.677
And I think that's one of the things

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.011
that we have going on in America

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:52.712
right now.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.046
You know,

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.381
we have lost respect in the offices

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.583
that people hold.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.150
And I think

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.151
that we should have respectful

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.286
conversations at all times.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.087
And when he says

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.189
that, he was just calling to question

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.791
the results of the election,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.525
initially claiming

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.359
he wasn't

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:09.062
asking you to find him anything,

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.096
that's obviously not true.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.665
We've all heard the call

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.636
Well, I gave him all the facts.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.339
He said in the call that there's 5000

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.140
dead people

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.541
that were alleged to have voted.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.843
They sued us on 10,315.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.178
And I told them that there was two

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.579
and we found two more.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.148
They said that there's underage voters.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.282
66,000.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.216
There were zero,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.618
that there are thousands of felons.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.286
There was less than 74

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.221
2400 non-registered voters.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.056
There's actually zero.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:37.590
But Caitlin,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.691
what's really interesting is

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.860
I didn't realize until just recently,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.662
but it was reported in the newspaper

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.130
that he actually had paid

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.798
Berkeley Research Group.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.333
He spent over $600,000

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.935
for them to look into this.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.303
And he had that report the day

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.504
before he called.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.705
And then just a few weeks ago,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.339
we heard about

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:57.343
he paid simpatico about $750,000.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.912
And they also came back and said

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.813
there was not sufficient enough fraud

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.582
to overturn this race.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.218
So he had the facts and then he called.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.085
And that was a report

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.120
from The Washington Post.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.622
And so he had those facts. He called you.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.524
You explained again to him

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.725
the numbers

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.294
But do you believe he was strong

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.196
arming you in

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.298
using your office to get him votes that

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.666
he did not earn from voters?

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.535
Well, I knew that

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.571
we didn't have the votes.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.205
We knew that we had

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.039
checked out everything,

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.674
every single allegation.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.441
In fact,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.443
he handpicked Bobby Christin, his U.S.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.878
attorney from the Southern District,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.146
to come up to Atlanta

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.147
and specifically

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.815
look at the Fulton County

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:36.950
counting of the absentee

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.252
ballots that went on on election night.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.853
And Bobbi Kristina as a youth attorney

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.421
acting U.S.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.922
attorney of the northern district,

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:43.890
did not find,

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.091
you know, fraud there

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.192
and then report that back

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.393
to the president.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.461
And so every time

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.562
that there was an allegation,

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.930
we did our checking

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.399
so we could report back to the voters.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.002
We report I report back to the voters.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.537
I want to all the voters understand

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.204
that we're going to be fair

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.305
and honest election.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.007
And that's my job.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:01.441
To make sure

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.376
that they have confidence in the results.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.477
What do you make of him saying

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.478
that he would make that

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.013
same call again to you today

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.915
despite the fact that the d.A.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.384
There said charges could come this summer

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.689
well, if he did, he'd get the same answer

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.223
that now

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.058
we have even more data points

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.059
that just show

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.095
that president trump did come up short.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.630
So what happened in Georgia?

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.631
And I think it may have happened

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.432
in other states, but in georgia, we know.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.101
24,000 voters

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.036
skipped the presidential race.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.471
They didn't vote for any of the three

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.972
candidates for president

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.807
and yet they voted down ballot

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:35.942
in other races.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.542
And that's why

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.344
president trump came up short.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:38.711
In fact,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.379
what you saw

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:39.979
is actually

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.515
our Republican congressman got 33,000

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.783
more votes collectively,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.918
33,000 more votes than President Trump.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.421
You've been clear

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.422
that you obviously follow

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.757
the numbers there, but you say,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.891
I am a Republican.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:52.425
You've noted

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.393
before that you would have wanted

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.094
a Republican to win that election.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.195
Does it hurt Republicans

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.864
to have someone who is right now

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.132
the GOP frontrunner

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.400
that is still denying

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.968
the results of the election, including in

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:02.635
your state

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.873
I think that when people

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.640
run for office,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.108
they should be looking forward

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.742
because that's where we going

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.144
to spend our future time.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.478
And that's really where

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:13.346
what people are looking at,

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.947
what's going to happen next week,

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.015
what's going to happen next year?

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.784
What are your plans for the future?

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.085
And so I think that

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.320
when people run campaigns

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.054
that should be really

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:22.121
looking towards the future

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.589
not just looking back

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.825
and talking about stolen election claims

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.927
which have been disproven.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.929
Brad Raffensperger, Georgia's Republican

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.230
secretary of state, your name was invoked

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.298
many times last night.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.399
So thank you for joining us and

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.101
your time tonight.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.136
Thank you.

